Proper lighting has always been essential to productivity.

311
00:26:19,021 --> 00:26:27,180
Until the early part of the 20th century, lighting, natural lighting, influenced the very design of the building itself.

312
00:26:28,840 --> 00:26:37,500
Workspaces were lit principally by daylight so that the close proximity to windows was extremely important for the quality of space.

313
00:26:38,220 --> 00:26:45,440
At the turn of the 20th century, Chicago architects designed central courtyards that allowed light into the center of the structure.

314
00:26:45,441 --> 00:26:52,280
In New York, architects designed tall, slender towers.

315
00:26:54,620 --> 00:26:59,460
Appearing in both cities were buildings with indentations for better access to light.

316
00:27:03,800 --> 00:27:11,040
And it was the incandescent electric bulb, Edison, 1879, that changed everything.

317
00:27:11,041 --> 00:27:18,040
And it was during the 1880s that electric lighting began to come into use on a commercial basis.

318
00:27:19,840 --> 00:27:22,380
Edison didn't actually invent the light bulb.

319
00:27:22,960 --> 00:27:27,280
He invented a less expensive, longer-lasting, and more reliable light bulb.

320
00:27:29,720 --> 00:27:34,540
He also patented switches, outlets, and sockets to support his light.

321
00:27:35,280 --> 00:27:38,320
Thomas Edison realized the light bulb needed electricity.

322
00:27:38,321 --> 00:27:42,780
And there was not any power generating plants at that time.

323
00:27:43,460 --> 00:27:46,460
So while he had a great invention, there was nothing to plug it into.

324
00:27:47,700 --> 00:27:53,760
On September 4, 1882, Edison's Pearl Street plant opened in Lower Manhattan,

325
00:27:54,740 --> 00:27:58,060
becoming the country's first commercial electrical generating station.

326
00:28:00,460 --> 00:28:02,920
Built in the heart of New York's financial district,

327
00:28:02,921 --> 00:28:07,520
the plant initially provided electricity for lighting to 59 customers.

328
00:28:07,521 --> 00:28:09,760
in a one-square-mile area.

329
00:28:12,760 --> 00:28:14,380
Just two decades later,

330
00:28:15,020 --> 00:28:16,520
large buildings throughout the country

331
00:28:16,521 --> 00:28:19,180
were using electricity to run lights and elevators.

332
00:28:22,380 --> 00:28:25,140
The early electric lights were more for task lighting

333
00:28:25,141 --> 00:28:26,140
than room illumination.

334
00:28:27,640 --> 00:28:30,220
But the shape of things started to change

335
00:28:30,221 --> 00:28:32,100
with the introduction of fluorescent lighting

336
00:28:32,101 --> 00:28:33,600
in the late 1930s.

337
00:28:34,400 --> 00:28:36,780
After the invention of fluorescent light,

338
00:28:36,781 --> 00:28:43,880
The internal space of the office could be much deeper than it was before because fluorescent lights are cool.

339
00:28:44,160 --> 00:28:49,540
So you didn't need to have any longer the light wells that cut into the space.

