355
00:30:01,780 --> 00:30:06,180
If you use half of the amount of energy, you also spend half the amount of money every year.

356
00:30:06,960 --> 00:30:11,700
And with big buildings, those are several hundred thousand dollars of savings every year.

357
00:30:15,300 --> 00:30:19,760
The one Bryant Park building in Manhattan will have another cool way of saving money.

358
00:30:21,980 --> 00:30:25,120
Because electricity rates fluctuate throughout the day and night,

359
00:30:25,940 --> 00:30:29,700
Power is more expensive during peak demand, usually midday.

360
00:30:31,120 --> 00:30:36,940
The One Bryant Park building will maximize its electricity usage through a system called off-peak cooling.

361
00:30:38,280 --> 00:30:45,980
In Manhattan, we stress out the electrical infrastructure on very hot days in the middle of summer all at the same time.

362
00:30:46,380 --> 00:30:48,220
And it's just incredibly inefficient.

363
00:30:49,040 --> 00:30:52,660
So one of the unique technologies that's happening here is called ice storage.

364
00:30:52,661 --> 00:30:56,620
In the middle of the night, when there's very little stress on the infrastructure,

365
00:30:56,960 --> 00:30:59,860
we're going to use chillers to make ice all night long,

366
00:30:59,920 --> 00:31:02,600
like a chipmunk storing nuts for the lean times.

367
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:05,980
And then in the peak of the day, we actually have cold stored up.

368
00:31:07,020 --> 00:31:10,540
Inside each large tank are dozens of spiral tubes,

369
00:31:11,040 --> 00:31:12,220
